	<key>readme</key>
	<string># Character &amp; Word Counter

Count characters, words, lines, and bytes of any text in Alfred.

## Requirements

- [Alfred 5](https://www.alfredapp.com/) with the Powerpack
- macOS (uses the system `zsh` only — no PHP, Python, or Homebrew deps)

## Usage

### Keyword

1. Type `cw` (configurable) followed by a space and your text.
2. Alfred shows live counts: characters, words, characters without whitespace, lines, and UTF-8 bytes.
3. Press **↩** on a row to copy that number.
4. Press **⌘↩** to copy and paste into the frontmost app.

### Universal Action

1. Select text in any app.
2. Trigger Alfred's Universal Actions hotkey.
3. Choose **Character &amp; Word Counter**.
4. Pick a metric and copy (or ⌘↩ to paste).

## Configuration

Open the workflow → **Configure Workflow…** to change the keyword (default `cw`).

## Credits

- Icon: [Flaticon](https://www.flaticon.com/free-icon/alphabet-letters-a-b-and-c_27482)
</string>
